<section class="section section--mist" aria-labelledby="why-local-h">
  <div class="wrap split">
    <div>
      <h2 id="why-local-h">Why the city on your website matters</h2>
      <p>When someone searches "roofer near me" or "basement renovation Whitby", Google matches the search to pages that name that service and that city. A homepage that only says "serving the GTA" rarely ranks against a competitor whose page names the town by name.</p>
      <p>That's why every website we build, from Starter to Growth, is written for your actual service area, not a generic template swapped with a different city name.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h2>One business per trade, per city</h2>
      <p>We only take on one business per trade in each city we serve, so the website and local SEO work we do for you isn't competing with a client we built the same thing for down the street.</p>
      <p>Want local SEO on top of your website? See <a href="/google-business-profile/">Google Business Profile management</a>, built to get you ranking in the map pack for your city.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

